I know the feeling but... as a general rule, don't go to the
monsters; let them come to you.  Even without a 'trice corpse:
Valks are fast; if the monster comes to you, you generally get
two free hits.  If you're a legal Valk, dual weaponing Excalibur
and something else that's good (another long sword, or a
katana), that's often enough.  I used to use 'trice corpses
whenever I could---I got the same rush from them you describe--,
but I now tend to think of them as a special case.  For
instance, if you're up against a demon who keeps teleporting to
the up stairs... but is foolish enough to generate a swarm of
monsters with a 'trice which leaves a corpse.  In most cases,
they rather bother me---unless there's a hoard attacking, I'm
not going to use it, and I'm always a little bit worried that
someone else will.

